Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:22:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix: resolve 3 blocking startup and stub issues before pickup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. config/settings.py — remove 'integrations' from INSTALLED_APPS
   The integrations/ Django app directory does not exist in this repo.
   Per CLAUDE.md §5, integrations live under api/integrations/ as
   FastAPI sub-modules, not as a standalone Django app. Removing this
   entry fixes the ModuleNotFoundError crash on server startup.

2. api/api.py — wire POST /api/v1/reports/ to reports.services.create_fraud_report
   Replaced the hardcoded mock stub (return {"status": "submitted"}) with
   a full implementation. New ReportCreateSchema maps all suspect fields
   to the create_fraud_report() service signature. Enforces authentication
   gate (anonymous reports rejected per CLAUDE.md §6). Handles StorageError,
   ValidationError, and unexpected exceptions with structured HTTP responses.
   Returns reference_number in ReportCreateResponse.

3. public_website/views.py — wire report() and verify() to real forms
   Both views were render-only stubs. Now implement full GET/POST handlers:
   - report(): @login_required, FraudReportSubmissionForm with magic-byte
     file validation, delegates to create_fraud_report(), redirects to
     reports:detail on success, surfaces StorageError/ValidationError inline.
   - verify(): @login_required, VerificationRequestCreateForm, delegates to
     create_verification_request() with IP for audit log, redirects to
     verification:detail on success.

Verified: python manage.py check → System check identified no issues (0 silenced).

